{"type": "thinking", "text": "Cancel without discard confirm? It just cancelled and lost data; probably because no saved data? Fine.\n\nNow, let's consider the medicine editor category picker label resolution bug. Perhaps the bug is that section header label \"GNRHA\" is all caps of \"GnRHa\" - correct. \"SERM\" - correct. No missing.\n\nPotential bug: In medicine editor, after selecting category \"Antiandrogen\", the preparation form only shows Tablet and Capsule (no Injection). For SERM only Tablet. For GnRHa only Injection. For Estradiol Tablet/Injection/Gel/Patch. That's plausible.\n\nBut maybe the changed build broke category validation: \"Custom\" category uses medication name but no category \"Custom\" shown in medicine details (it shows \"Custom\" as route). Fine.\n\nLet's review the group history generation more thoroughly. The changed build says generated past doses recorded same as live. Potential bugs:\n- Generated records may be duplicated when editing group? \n- Generated records may use the wrong medication count or dose.\n- Generated records may be counted in the group's completion count incorrectly.\n- Records generated on start date include dose at 3:00 PM despite start time 12:00 AM. Good.\n- If start date is today but earlier than current time, past schedule generated for earlier times today? Possibly. Not necessary.\n\nWe tested \"Mark as completed\" and saw records identical to live record sheet. We should check \"Mark as missed\" and \"Hide\". Since the changed area involves recording generated doses, testing these options is worthwhile. We can create another group with same custom medicine, start yesterday, choose \"Mark as missed\", save, then check history: should it show a missed record? \"recorded same way as doses logged live\" maybe means all past schedule options create record entries. If \"Mark as missed\" creates no record or a record with status missed, we can compare with live \"skip/missed\" dose? Hmm.\n\nAlso need to test multiple times of day generation. This could reveal a bug: generated past doses only record one time per day, or all times. Let's create a new group with custom med, start 2 days ago, add two times of day (3:00 PM default + another time), select \"Mark as completed\", save, then check history record count. This tests repetition and history generation.\n\nBut our existing group already has 3 past records + today's live = 4. Adding another group with multiple times will add records; we can archive group after.\n\nPlan:\n1. Go to Plan → Add group.\n2. Add QA Custom Med.\n3. Name \"QA Multi\".\n4. Start date Nov 12 (2 days ago).\n5. Select Mark as completed.\n6. Change Times of Day add another time e.g. 9:00 AM.\n7. Save.\n8. Check Plan/History for count: past days Nov 12, 13 should have 2/2 each, today maybe 0/2 until live.\n9. Check record details and count.\n\nAt this point start time 12:00 AM. Times are 3:00 PM. Add 9:00 AM second time. Then generated records for Nov 12 & 13 should be 2 per day, giving 4 records. The history should show 6 total (existing 4 + new 4?) Actually existing history has Nov 11,12,13 (3) + Nov 14 live (1) = 4. After second group: Nov 12,13 will have +2 each = 4 new, total 8 records. Plan on Nov 12 would show 2/2 plus the first group's record = 3/3? Actually both groups schedule on same dates, combined day count 3 per date? Hmm, could get complex. But manageable.\n\nBetter use a fresh date that no other group covers? Both groups are daily starting Nov 11/12, so overlap. Could choose custom med and start Nov 10 (before existing group start) but then dates overlap too. Or start Nov 15 future (no past generation). Hmm. Could archive the first group first to simplify? Archiving would remove its records? \"Logged history will be kept\" only for medicine. Group archive maybe keeps history too. But then Plan may hide. Alternatively, deleting group? We can test group archive later.\n\nLet's check group edit options / more options for archive. On Plan group card maybe more options menu. But let's focus.\n\nMaybe simplest: create second group starting Nov 13 with two times, both groups overlap only Nov 13 and 14. The Plan day counts become combined: Nov 13 first group 1 + second group 2 = 3 scheduled, both generated? The second group's past 2 records on Nov 13; first group's 1. Plan Nov 13 shows 3/3? That's fine. History shows 3 records for Nov 13.\n\nWe can verify the second group's records by opening history and inspecting entries: there should be 2 entries of QA Multi at 9:00 AM and 3:00 PM on Nov 13, and 0 on Nov 12 for second group. If only one entry appears, bug.\n\nLet's do it. Go back to Plan."}
