{"type": "thinking", "text": "Portrait Plan looks fine, no overlap; nav bar floats over content (by design). The \"Sublingual|Home\" merge is just accessibility grouping of overlapping floating nav with card behind. Not a bug.\n\nNow, we've done a lot. Are there any actual bugs found? So far none. We need to dig into the changed features more deeply. Let's reconsider.\n\nChanged:\n1. Medicine editor category picker: category labels now resolved from shared string resources.\n2. Lab test results under Calibration: units for each test now fetched together with the test list.\n3. Group editor history generation: generated past doses now recorded same way as doses logged live.\n\nPotential subtle bugs:\n1. Category labels may be wrong when locale or string resources? We tested all labels: Estradiol, Antiandrogen, SERM, GnRHa, Custom. They displayed correctly in picker and section headers. But the medicine list line shows route (Oral/Injection), which seems deliberate.\n\nMaybe the bug is the \"Custom\" category chip label is correct but when selected, the \"Medication\" section absent; not a bug.\n\n2. Units fetched with test list: We saw each test's unit chips. But maybe the bug is a unit appears for a test that shouldn't, or selected default unit mismatches. We saw defaults: Estradiol pg/mL, Testosterone ng/dL, Progesterone ng/mL, Prolactin ng/mL, FSH mIU/mL, LH mIU/mL. All correct.\n\nCould there be a bug when the same unit is shared between tests? For example \"ng/mL\" appears for Testosterone, Progesterone, Prolactin but each selection should be independent. We could test: add Testosterone with ng/mL and Progesterone with nmol/L; verify selected chips don't bleed. In our saved result, Testosterone ng/dL and FSH mIU/mL; units are independent. We saw when we changed Estradiol to pmol/L, only its target changed; no bleed. Good.\n\n3. Generated past doses recorded as live: We saw records with same fields, counts. One interesting thing: when a group is created with a past start date, the generated doses are recorded with \"Scheduled for\" label. Same as live. The medication amounts? The record sheet does not show dose count (tablets per dose), neither for live. So consistent.\n\nMaybe the bug: generated past doses are marked \"on track\" even though the group's schedule says \"Mark as completed\" vs \"Mark as missed\". In history the legend has On track, Partial, Missed, Off plan. The generated completed records should be \"On track\". We didn't inspect the calendar color indicators, but likely.\n\nMaybe a bug: after creating a group with past start, the records count on the Plan date \"1/1\" includes generated records, good.\n\nMaybe the bug: when editing/deleting generated records, the Plan shows \"MISSED\" as we saw. That's consistent.\n\nCould be a bug when editing a generated record's time or date: The record's group association remains, and the record maybe moves? Not necessarily.\n\nLet's inspect the group \"PAST SCHEDULE\" behavior for a start time earlier today. The group editor \"START TIME Now\" vs date. If start date is in the past, it sets time to 12:00 AM, but if you choose today and start time is \"Now\", and the current time is 2:48 PM, the 3:00 PM dose is future, no past schedule. If you set start time to 9:00 AM today, then past schedule for today's 3pm? No, 3pm is future. If time of day 9:00 AM, then past schedule would generate a 9am dose today. Could test to ensure generated past doses for today are recorded. But not necessary.\n\nPotential major bug: The group's \"START TIME\" when selecting a past start date resets to 12:00 AM, and generated doses are at 3pm. Fine.\n\nLet's look for issue in the medicine category picker with \"Custom\" category. Maybe selecting Custom then switching back to Estradiol loses state or shows stale fields. We saw switching among categories updates fields. Let's test rapid switches with values typed: type custom name, switch to Antiandrogen, switch back to Custom, see if custom name retained or reset. This tests state. But maybe user would expect reset. Not a bug.\n\nAnother angle: Medicine categories are label-resolved. The section headers in medicine list show \"GNRHA\" correct. But perhaps some category labels are missing in the \"medication details\" or \"group card\" where \"Custom\" route displayed. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the bug is in the medicine list sorting or category display: The first medicine \"Estradiol valerate\" under header ESTRADIOL shows \"Oral\". If the item's subtitle is supposed to be category, then it's wrong. But given Antiandrogen tablet also \"Oral\", it must be route. So the line is route.\n\nActually wait: the medicine list item shows \"Category | Name | form · strength\". The first line might be the \"route\", which for Oral tablets is \"Oral\". For custom, route might not be set and falls back to category \"Custom\". That's plausible. But is the route shown for custom supposed to be \"Custom\"? It says \"Custom\" twice in the item (section header CUSTOM, item \"Custom\"). That's acceptable.\n\nLet's look at the group card medication chip for Estradiol valerate (Sublingual) - it shows \"Estradiol valerate · Sublingual · 2 mg\". So route is displayed as Sublingual. Custom shows \"QA Custom Med · Custom · 5 μg\". So route for custom is \"Custom\" (a placeholder). Fine.\n\nCould there be an issue with the medicine editor preset doses: selecting a preset fills strength but display name hint maybe remains. We tested 2mg saved correctly.\n\nWhat about editing an existing medicine's strength? Does it persist and reflect in group card? We can test edit medicine strength to 3 mg and verify. But this may affect group card. Let's test quickly:\n- Go Medicines, open Estradiol valerate, edit strength 2 → 4, save, check group card shows 4 mg. Then maybe revert to 2.\nThis tests persistence. We can do it.\n\nBut maybe more valuable: test the lab test results persistence across navigation and app restart? We can't restart app (open_app only foregrounds). We navigated away and back; persisted.\n\nLet's test opening Calibration via a different route: Settings > Calibration vs maybe Home? Not needed.\n\nLet's inspect Calibration \"3 available\" issue: When adding a test result, the available count is 4 initially; after adding Progesterone, 3 available. Fine.\n\nPotential bug: After we added custom analyte SHBG, the default unit for the custom analyte is shown as nmol/L and only one option. But when editing a result that includes SHBG, does it show the unit? We didn't save a result with SHBG. Could be a bug if units fetched with test list fail for custom analytes. But we confirmed Add result sheet shows \"SHBG - nmol/L\" and the form shows nmol/L chip. Good.\n\nWait, after adding SHBG to calibration settings, the summary card \"+1 record\" maybe wrong? Earlier we added FSH, making 3 tests but card showed +1 record. Let's check: The card screenshot showed \"150 pg/mL Estradiol\", \"+1 record\", \"40 ng/dL Testosterone\". It didn't show FSH as a third line but \"+1 record\" indicates 1 more. Good. But now the history record count says 5. Fine.\n\nLet's examine the result edit sheet and \"in range\" badges:\n- Estradiol 150 pg/mL target 100-200 => In range. good.\n- Testosterone 40 ng/dL target <50 => In range. good.\n- FSH 5 mIU/mL no target => no badge.\n- If value out of range, should show High/Low. Test with Estradiol 300. We can edit the saved result and set 300, check badge \"High\". Then maybe set back to 150. This tests validation/consistency. Let's do it; could reveal target range unit conversion bug.\n\nOpen Calibration. Go Settings → Calibration."}
