t selector changes the unit label and target range but does not convert the entered value. But maybe it's intentional: the user is telling the app \"this result is 150 in the new unit\" and must re-enter the value. But converting is more expected.\n\nHmm. The task says \"Lab test results under Calibration: the units for each test are now fetched together with the test list.\" This changed area focuses on units being fetched with the test list. A likely bug could be the units not being applied correctly when editing results or when changing preferred units. Let's investigate more concretely.\n\nThe summary card displays 550.6 pmol/L while the edit form shows 150 pg/mL. That's not wrong. But if we change the unit chip in the edit from pg/mL to pmol/L and save, what happens? Previously we did that (when settings were pg/mL) and then switched back before saving. Let's see if switching unit and saving with same value stores a different canonical value. Then summary would show something else. But this is a semantics question.\n\nMaybe the more clear-cut bug: The edit form's unit selection is not respecting the preferred unit setting. If settings say pmol/L, the result list shows pmol/L, but the edit shows pg/mL. Hmm, but the record was stored with pg/mL; maybe per-result unit. Actually the unit chips are part of the result record. The settings default unit only applies to new results. The list display uses the preferred unit though. Hmm, or maybe the list display uses the per-record unit? But it changed to 550.6 when we changed the default, so list uses preferred unit, not record unit. That suggests the record unit is not stored, and the value is stored canonical. Then why does the edit show 150 pg/mL? It might convert back to the unit with which the record was originally entered? Or it's a bug that the edit doesn't convert.\n\nLet's test carefully:\n1. Current state: settings preferred Estradiol = pmol/L. Summary card = 550.6 pmol/L.\n2. Edit shows 150 pg/mL. If I switch