{"type": "thinking", "text": "Maybe a bug: The target for Testosterone in nmol/L is \"<1.7 nmol/L\", which is a rounding of 1.735. Fine.\n\nLet's reconsider category labels: maybe the *section header* text uses uppercase labels, and the *medicine item* first line \"Oral\" might actually be the \"category\" label because the medicine's category is inferred from route? Wait, we selected category \"Estradiol\" but the section header is \"ESTRADIOL\". The first line \"Oral\" is route. Good.\n\nLet's test adding a custom medicine with a different form (Capsule) and unit \"g\" and see if route is \"Custom\" or \"Oral\". Probably \"Custom\". Not relevant.\n\nWhat about the category label resolution for \"SERM\" not being styled consistently? The chip \"SERM\" is four letters; no issue.\n\nCould the shared string resources cause the labels to show *the same string for multiple categories* under some conditions? We saw distinct.\n\nMaybe if the app is restarted, the category labels are unresolved (e.g., show empty). We can't restart the app fully, but we can force-stop? There is no tool to force-stop. Could use open_app (foreground only) not reset. We could kill via recents? Press APP_SWITCH and swipe app away, then open_app. That's effectively a restart. Is that allowed? The instructions say \"open_app (does not reset its data)\" and \"Fresh install ...\". We can test state across app restart by swiping the app away from recents and reopening. That could reveal persistence issues. Let's try: press APP_SWITCH, swipe the app card away, then open_app. But this might end the QA session? No, just the app. Data persisted in DB. Could be valuable to test persistence of all our data.\n\nBut risk: the tool session may lose the app? open_app will bring it back. Let's do it near the end after we finish.\n\nLet's look for bugs in the \"Group editor history generation\" by checking the group editor's PAST SCHEDULE preview for a future group—no. Maybe \"Hide\" leaves generated records? We verified no extra entry on Plan and history count unchanged (we didn't explicitly compare history count after hidden group, but we saw Plan didn't show it). Let's verify history count still 5 after hidden group. Open history and check. That's quick.\n\nGo Plan already? We're in Calibration. Go back to Settings then Plan. Use back arrow (element 8)."}
